# Keep everything but addons/nightfox/ out of the archives GitHub generates
# (`git archive`, the release "Source code (zip)", /archive/*.zip).
#
# That zip is what people feed to Godot's asset installer, which strips the single
# top-level folder and writes the rest into res:// verbatim -- it has no special
# case for project.godot. Anything left at archive root therefore OVERWRITES the
# target project's file of that name. addons/nightfox/ carries its own README and
# LICENSE, so the installed tree stays self-describing.
/project.godot      export-ignore
/README.md          export-ignore
/LICENSE            export-ignore
/demo.gd            export-ignore
/demo.gd.uid        export-ignore
/generator          export-ignore
/.gitattributes     export-ignore
/.gitignore         export-ignore
